      "text": "Bot accounting needs explicit profit and cost definitions. Freqtrade combines realized and unrealized profit and includes fees; Hummingbot documents performance relative to a hold portfolio. GIPS supplies a reference for separating external cash-flow effects from investment performance. Kraken ledger records distinguish funds movements from trades. Historical issue discussions and a grid-bot critique show why monitor figures need reconciliation and why a reported discrepancy must retain its attribution and scope.",
